//! The functions of masks, which take a simd struct of any type.
//!
//! `select(mask, a, b)` gives the lane of `a` where the lane of `mask` holds
//! and the lane of `b` where it does not. `any(mask)` holds when one lane of
//! `mask` holds, and `all(mask)` when every lane does. A comparison of two
//! values of a `simd struct` gives the mask. No function of Anti takes a value
//! of any type, so the compiler knows the three by name, and this module
//! declares nothing.
